# welcome-loop-load (H10): route welcome from load, no navigation. The port's
# loop starts at frame 0; the reference mounts the page some frames after
# load (React's first render and effects), so the two loops start offset.
# Model loop_at values: 1800 -> x2 k -1.14; 2420 -> x2 k -1.50 (the k drag
# ends at 2416.67). The phase-1 probe measured the real-clock mount delay
# (first rAF callback after load: chromium ~106 ms, webkit ~267 ms, firefox
# ~389 ms); the run fits the offset from the curve's k, recorded as category
# (e) with the number — the loop starts at mount on both sides, so no code
# change can match it.
size 1440 900
density 2
scheme dark
mode dark
theme arctic-ice
route welcome
wait 1800
shot loop-load-1800
wait 620
shot loop-load-2420
